        <mxCell id="n38" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" value="FINDING F1 (High). Zero-priest agyari: the booking is created at status=requested with NO BookingMobed and NO notification to anyone (services no longer notify admins). The behdin is told &#39;request has been sent&#39;. It can never be accepted — accept/decline requires a BookingMobed row. The request silently dies. Code comments admit it is &#39;out of scope&#39;, but it is a live false-confirmation." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="320" x="1120" y="1235" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e39" edge="1" parent="1" source="n15" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="n38" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n40" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" value="FINDING B2 (Med). Services picker and priest picker are dynamic WhatsApp Flows. Same simulator gap as B1 (unrenderable in /chat) AND the priest step only accepts &#39;priest_&lt;id&gt;&#39; text — no name synonyms — so a multi-priest booking is untestable by hand without internal user ids. Also needs Flow registration + keys (all empty in repo)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="175" width="330" x="1060" y="155" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e41" edge="1" parent="1" source="n2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=1;exitY=0.4;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="n40" value="">
